WHY NON-COMMERCIAL, WHEN THE CODE IS NOT
----------------------------------------
This is a deliberate asymmetry, not an oversight.

The schematics are depictions of Rupiah banknotes. They exist under the
educational exemption in UU 7/2011 Pasal 24 ayat (1), which permits imitating
Rupiah for educational and/or promotional purposes with the word "spesimen"
applied. That exemption attaches to the purpose of the use, and Pasal 24 ayat (2)
separately prohibits distributing or circulating Rupiah Tiruan.

A permissive licence on the artwork would invite reuse whose purpose this project
cannot see and cannot vouch for. Restricting commercial reuse keeps the artwork
closer to the exemption it relies on. The code carries no such risk, so it is
MIT and genuinely open source.

Note that CC BY-NC-SA is not an OSI-approved open-source licence. The artwork is
"open" in the sense of freely readable, shareable, and adaptable for education —
not in the OSI sense.

NOTHING HERE GRANTS RIGHTS OVER RUPIAH ITSELF
---------------------------------------------
This licence covers only original work in this repository. It grants no rights
in respect of Indonesian currency, and it does not exempt anyone from UU 7/2011.
Any reuse of the schematics must keep the SPESIMEN marking intact and remain
within the statutory exemption. Removing the marking is not a licence violation
so much as a criminal one.

Bank Indonesia is not affiliated with this project and has not endorsed it.
